<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Existing Samplers Benefit from Greedy-Threshold</h3>

<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Majority voted results on GSM8K. In addition to existing sampling conditions, Greedy-Threshold <math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{GT}=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{GT}=0.3</annotation></semantics></math> is applied. Greedy-Threshold improves majority voting performance, especially in models with lower starting accuracy. Statistically significant differences (<math id="S4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>) marked in <span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.</figcaption>
